        "markdown": "# Markdown Sample\n\nThis sample covers headings, lists, a table, links, a blockquote, and code.\n\n## Lists and Tasks\n\n### Nested bullets\n\n- Frontend\n  - Components\n    - Buttons\n    - Forms\n  - Styling\n- Backend\n  - Routes\n\n1. Clone the repository\n2. Install dependencies\n3. Run the test suite\n\n- [x] Write the parser\n- [x] Add unit tests\n- [ ] Update the docs\n- [ ] Tag the release\n\n## Reference Table\n\n| Project | Language | Stars | License | Last Updated |\n| --- | --- | ---: | --- | --- |\n| remark | TypeScript | 6,200 | MIT | 2026-08-14 |\n| markdown-it | JavaScript | 8,900 | MIT | 2026-07-02 |\n| pulldown-cmark | Rust | 1,100 | MIT | 2026-09-21 |\n| goldmark | Go | 4,500 | MIT | 2026-06-30 |\n\n## Links and Hashes\n\nSee the [CommonMark specification](https://spec.commonmark.org/) for the full grammar.\n\nRaw link: https://github.com/commonmark/commonmark-spec\n\nCommit reference: `3f9a1c7e2b8d4560a1f3c9e7b2d8046f5a1c3e9b`\n\n> Markdown is a plain-text format, so the rendered output depends on the parser that reads it.\n\n---\n\n## Code\n\n```typescript\nconst user = await getUserProfile(request.userId, { includeTeams: true, scope: 'admin' });\nconsole.log(user.name);\n```",
